## Phase Verification Checklists

### Phase 1-5 (Build Verification)
- [ ] Individual services run successfully locally
- [ ] Docker images build without errors
- [ ] Individual service health checks pass
- [ ] docker-compose services start successfully
- [ ] All health endpoints return HTTP 200
- [ ] Model weights are mounted (not in image)
- [ ] No destructive commands used

### Phase 6 (Service Communication)
- [ ] Redis DB 0 (cache/session) communication verified
- [ ] Redis DB 1 (Celery broker) communication verified
- [ ] Redis DB 2 (Celery result) communication verified
- [ ] Backend → AI Server HTTP communication verified
- [ ] Backend → Media Server communication verified
- [ ] AI Server → Media Server communication verified
- [ ] Service name resolution works (ping tests)
- [ ] Port accessibility verified (nc tests)
- [ ] Error handling tested (service unavailable scenarios)
- [ ] End-to-end flow verified (video/image processing paths)

### Phase 7 (Logic Migration)
- [ ] Endpoint identified and categorized
- [ ] Test written before migration
- [ ] Legacy code copied and wrapped
- [ ] Dependencies updated (AI calls → HTTP client)
- [ ] Test passes after migration
- [ ] Manual API test successful
- [ ] Error handling preserved
- [ ] Response format matches legacy
- [ ] Documentation updated

### Phase 8 (Integration Testing)
- [ ] Unit tests written (service layer)
- [ ] Integration tests written (service-to-service)
- [ ] E2E tests written (complete flows)
- [ ] Error scenario tests written
- [ ] Performance tests written (query count, response time)
- [ ] All tests pass
- [ ] Test coverage >80% for service layer

### Phase 9 (Django Service Logic)
- [ ] Service layer pattern implemented (pipeline structure)
- [ ] AI client usage verified (HTTP, not direct calls)
- [ ] Transaction boundaries defined
- [ ] Error handling implemented (ServiceError mapping)
- [ ] Logging strategy implemented
- [ ] No prohibited patterns used
